From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: himax-spi: keep a tap locked while its signal collapses

The tap lock reports a touch at its down position until the touch
moves away. While the signal is under track_tap_fall percent of the
touch's peak, only a move past track_tap_hard (22 units, about 2.3 mm)
releases it. In the last one or two frames of a lift the centroid of
the fading signal still jumps that far, and the touch then reports the
jump; games that treat 10 pixels as a drag turn such a tap into a drag
or a flick.

Add track_tap_floor, default 35 percent: under it only twice
track_tap_hard releases the lock. A flick still has most of its signal
when it starts to move and is released as before. A finger that
pressed hard and then slides off lightly is released once it is twice
track_tap_hard away, which for the flicks in the recordings below was
one frame later. track_tap_hard is capped at 4096 units, the span of
the positions, so that twice it squared cannot overflow.

Checked with hxsim on five recorded rhythm-game sessions (about 5000
touches): taps whose raw centroid stayed within 1.5 mm but whose
reported point moved 10 units or more went from 129 of 2942 to 22.
Short flicks that never reported moving stayed at 17 of 716, and when
flicks start to move and when touches end did not change.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c |  2 ++
 drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c        | 19 +++++++++++++++----
 drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.h        |  6 +++++-
 3 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c
index 00601deef7..7d264238a2 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c
@@ -1137,6 +1137,7 @@ HX_ALGO_ATTR_S32_RW(track_tap_radius);
 HX_ALGO_ATTR_S32_RW(track_tap_speed);
 HX_ALGO_ATTR_S32_RW(track_tap_hard);
 HX_ALGO_ATTR_S32_RW(track_tap_fall);
+HX_ALGO_ATTR_S32_RW(track_tap_floor);
 HX_ALGO_ATTR_BOOL_RW(track_tap_snap);
 HX_ALGO_ATTR_S32_RW(track_filter_mincutoff);
 HX_ALGO_ATTR_S32_RW(track_filter_beta);
@@ -1295,6 +1296,7 @@ static struct attribute *hx_algo_attrs[] = {
 	&dev_attr_track_tap_speed.attr,
 	&dev_attr_track_tap_hard.attr,
 	&dev_attr_track_tap_fall.attr,
+	&dev_attr_track_tap_floor.attr,
 	&dev_attr_track_tap_snap.attr,
 	&dev_attr_track_filter_mincutoff.attr,
 	&dev_attr_track_filter_beta.attr,
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
index 9e58aefa57..0682fca173 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
@@ -97,6 +97,7 @@ void hx_algo_init_defaults(struct hx_algo *algo)
 	algo->track_tap_speed      = 15;   /* ~1.5 mm in one frame */
 	algo->track_tap_hard       = 22;   /* ~2.3 mm */
 	algo->track_tap_fall       = 50;
+	algo->track_tap_floor      = 35;
 	algo->track_tap_snap       = true;
 	algo->track_filter_mincutoff = 1000;  /* 1 Hz at rest */
 	algo->track_filter_beta      = 30;
@@ -2208,8 +2209,12 @@ static void hx_filter_update(const struct hx_algo *algo, struct hx_track *trk)
  * of a tap's centroid as the finger lifts, and so holds a flick back until it
  * has gone that far.  Two things tell the two apart.  The lifting centroid
  * jumps while the signal collapses: under track_tap_fall percent of the touch's
- * peak only track_tap_hard releases.  And once the landing has settled a tap
- * stays put, so a single step of track_tap_speed units is the finger moving.
+ * peak only track_tap_hard releases, and in the last frames of a lift, under
+ * track_tap_floor percent, only twice that.  A flick still has most of its
+ * signal when it starts to move; a finger that pressed hard and then slides off
+ * lightly is released once it is twice track_tap_hard away, a frame later for a
+ * flick.  And once the landing has settled a tap stays put, so a single step of
+ * track_tap_speed units is the finger moving.
  */
 static bool hx_track_left_anchor(const struct hx_algo *algo,
 				 const struct hx_track *trk)
@@ -2218,10 +2223,16 @@ static bool hx_track_left_anchor(const struct hx_algo *algo,
 	s64 ay = trk->y - trk->ref_y;
 	s64 d2 = ax * ax + ay * ay;
 	s64 r = algo->track_tap_radius;
-	s64 hard = max_t(s64, algo->track_tap_hard, r);
+	/* Positions span fewer than 4096 units: cap it there, so 4 * hard^2 fits. */
+	s64 hard = min_t(s64, max_t(s64, algo->track_tap_hard, r), 4096);
 	s64 v = algo->track_tap_speed;
 
-	if (r <= 0 || d2 > hard * hard)
+	if (r <= 0)
+		return true;
+	if (algo->track_tap_floor > 0 &&
+	    (s64)trk->signal_sum * 100 < (s64)algo->track_tap_floor * trk->sig_peak)
+		return d2 > 4 * hard * hard;
+	if (d2 > hard * hard)
 		return true;
 	if (algo->track_tap_fall > 0 &&
 	    (s64)trk->signal_sum * 100 < (s64)algo->track_tap_fall * trk->sig_peak)
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.h b/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.h
index d4f018d58f..5d7c8f2d75 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.h
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.h
@@ -392,7 +392,11 @@ struct hx_algo {
 	s32  track_tap_hard;       /* radius while the signal is falling   */
 				   /* (at least track_tap_radius)          */
 	s32  track_tap_fall;       /* falling: under this % of the touch's */
-				   /* peak signal (0 = ignore the signal)  */
+				   /* peak signal (0 = off; the floor      */
+				   /* below still applies)                 */
+	s32  track_tap_floor;      /* lifting: under this % of the peak    */
+				   /* only twice track_tap_hard releases   */
+				   /* (0 = off)                            */
 	bool track_tap_snap;       /* on release, report the contact       */
 				   /* itself, not the filter behind it     */
 	s32  track_filter_mincutoff; /* One Euro cutoff at rest, mHz (0 = off) */
